- U>G | ask for a week to think, and ask an actor you trust about the company | v: security, self-direction | tribal: ask an old teller who has been upriver what that band is like, before answering | magic: ask an old player what the company is really like, before answering | chance: 50
- B>W | put your name in the casting directory, now that a company has written | v: achievement, security | grants: casting directory listing | tribal: make sure every band at the gathering hears that a band upriver has sent word | magic: put your name on the brokers' roll, now that a company has sent word | chance: 90
- R>U | turn it down, but ask to sit in on their rehearsals and learn | v: self-direction, stimulation | self_control: + | tribal: send word you cannot come, but ask to watch their tellings at the gathering | magic: decline, but ask to watch the company rehearse when it passes through | chance: 48
- G>B | write back that you will come if the company finds work for your partner too | v: benevolence, security | binds | tribal: send word you will come if your partner's hearth can winter there too | magic: write back that you will come if the company takes your partner on as well | chance: 15
works: The answer goes back, and {N} never once regrets it in the year that follows.
works: By spring {N} is on the road with a company, learning the work from the inside.
fails: The company goes quiet after the first reply, and the part goes to someone else.
fails: Three weeks into the tour the money runs out, and {N} comes home with nothing but stories.
